1. Added proper initialization of start and end times using actual Date objects set to reasonable business hours (9 AM to 5 PM)
2. Ensured the form's defaultValues are properly structured with the correct schedule format
3. Added a wrapper div with padding for better visual presentation
4. Maintained all the existing props and structure while ensuring proper data initialization

This should resolve the "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'start')" error because we're now providing properly initialized Date objects for both start and end times in the form's default values.

The error was occurring because the TimeRangeField component was expecting properly formatted date objects for the start and end times, but our previous initialization wasn't providing them in the correct format. Now we're ensuring that the form is initialized with valid Date objects.

